## 2. Pokémon Reborn

*Pokémon Reborn* is a fan game by Amethyst and the Reborn development team.
The game itself is **not included in this repository**; obtain it from the
official site.

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `Scripts/**.rb` | Modified source of Pokémon Reborn / Pokémon Essentials. Only the files this patch changes are kept here, not the full tree. |
| `patch/Data/japanese.dat` | The translated message tables. Every entry is keyed by Reborn's original English line, so the file embeds the game's script. |
| `jp_translation/work/src/**`, `work/batch/**`, `work/answers/**` | The same text as editable sources — Reborn's complete English script alongside the translation. |
| `patch/Graphics/**` | Reborn's images with their embedded text repainted in Japanese. Derivative of the original art. |
| `jp_translation/backup/**` | Unmodified copies of Reborn's original scripts and message data, kept so the patch can be reverted. |

Translating and redistributing this material is done on the understanding that
it accompanies, and does not replace, the original game. **Confirm the Reborn
team's position before redistributing.**

## 3. Pokémon

*Pokémon* is a registered trademark of Nintendo, The Pokémon Company, GAME
FREAK and Creatures Inc. The translation uses the **official Japanese names**
of Pokémon, moves, abilities, items and types, and — for entries that exist in
the official games — official Japanese descriptive text. Those rights belong to
the companies above.

`jp_translation/tools/pokeapi_csv/` is **deliberately not committed**. It holds
that official text, and it is only an input to `build_glossary.py` and
`build_descriptions.py`. Both download it on demand from
<https://github.com/PokeAPI/pokeapi> when it is missing.

## 4. Bundled font — `patch/Fonts/pokemonemerald.ttf`

This replaces Reborn's font of the same name, which has no kana or kanji.

Its name table declares:

    Copyright (C) 2013 M+ Font Project
    Family      PokemonEmerald
    Unique ID   PokemonEmerald;JP
    Version     2013.0602

so the Japanese glyphs come from the **M+ FONTS Project**. The M+ license of
that era grants unlimited permission to use, copy, modify and redistribute the
fonts, commercially or not, with no warranty.

The file it replaces — Reborn's `Fonts/pokemonemerald.ttf` — declares:

    Copyright aztecwarrior28 2020
    "Pokémon Emerald Pro" by "crystalwalrein", built with FontStruct
    License     Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike
                http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

The bundled file carries the same family name and adds Japanese glyphs to that
design, so it appears to combine M+ glyphs with the FontStruct *PokemonEmerald*
face. Both are credited here on that basis.

**Unverified:** the bundled file itself states no license, and its exact
provenance is unknown to this project. If the CC BY-SA 3.0 terms reach the
Latin glyphs, the ShareAlike condition attaches to the font. Verify before
redistributing the font outside this patch.

Credits, regardless of which terms apply:

